======================  THE TRAP ROOM  ======================

So. You found the hidden door. Clever.

But the cleverness that got you IN will not get you OUT.

This room punishes the careless. Two temptations sit in plain sight:

  1. A « cursed_chest » -- shiny, obvious, begging to be opened.
  2. An open door marked « dead_end » -- a path that invites you in.

BOTH are bait. Open or enter them blindly and the trap will spring.

(Fear not -- every trap here is an illusion of the dungeon.

 Nothing on your real disk will ever be harmed or deleted.)

The dungeon's oldest rule still holds:

  * INSPECT before you act. Identify things first:
        « file * »
        « head -n 1 cursed_chest »
    If you see a '#!', it is a script -- know what it does before you run it.

  * The TRUE way out is not in plain sight.
    Brighten your torch to find what is hidden:
        « ls -a »

Find the hidden clue. Confirm it is safe. THEN use it.

That is how the careful escape -- and how the careless are trapped.
